      "severity": "P1",
      "title": "Prevent attempt identity reuse after checkpoint recovery",
      "file": "core.mjs",
      "line": 358,
      "reason": "Attempts increment only the checkpoint-local counter. Reproduced: save a pending checkpoint at attempt 0; execute and complete attempt 1; restore the older checkpoint; reconcile it through the trusted host; start another execution. Its counter becomes 1 again, so finishStep accepts the original attempt-1 receipt and delivery reports complete without a new result. This violates requirements.md:27 and 53 and can falsely certify retried operations. Allocate execution identities from trusted monotonic attempt records or a fresh execution nonce bound into receipts. Validate by replaying an old receipt after restoring an older checkpoint and requiring rejection."
    },
    {
      "severity": "P1",
      "title": "Validate completed receipts against their recorded attempt",
      "file": "core.mjs",
      "line": 183,
      "reason": "stepEvidence checks execution_attempt only when its optional argument is supplied; nextAction validates completed stages without it. Reproduced: complete attempts 1 and 2, import a completed checkpoint whose evidence_ids reference the still-attested attempt-1 receipt, and provide current host recovery reconciliation. nextAction reports complete despite the stored counter being 2 and without explicit host.reuse. Imported Task Context therefore selects historical results outside the required reuse path (requirements.md:27). Check completed receipts against the recorded execution identity; separately bind explicit reuse decisions. Validate that this imported mismatch blocks while authorized explicit reuse still succeeds."
    },
    {
      "severity": "P2",
      "title": "Check demonstrated input changes before returning unknown coverage",
      "file": "core.mjs",
      "line": 55,
      "reason": "The early coverage/environment return prevents inspection of known dependency changes. A non-mutating probe supplied an attested failed-test record with empty environment metadata and a core.mjs binding different from current content; evidenceValidity returned unknown instead of stale. unresolvedFailures consequently keeps this historical failure blocking execution and delivery, contrary to requirements.md:25 and 27. Preserve coverage uncertainty while checking available bindings for demonstrated changes before choosing unknown. Validate with a changed dependency plus missing environment metadata, and retain unknown when no input change is established."
    }
  ],
  "summary": "Independently checked repository conformance, intent fidelity and operational safety against AGENTS.md, requirements.md, contracts.md and contracts.skill.yaml. No separate conformance violation found; intent and safety findings are deduplicated above. Reviewed core.mjs as the fixed file scope and existing-tests.mjs as context. Native Node probes reproduced all three findings. Existing tests were not executed because their imports do not resolve and they perform prohibited writes/process execution. No files modified, Shell commands or network requests used. Host integration remains unverified. Add focused regressions for these failure sequences before acceptance."
